#!/usr/bin/env bash

# !!! WARNING !!!  This "chest" is a MIMIC -- a trap in disguise.
# If you are reading this with 'cat' or 'head', well done: you INSPECTED
# before opening. That is exactly how you survive this room.
# Running it springs the trap (harmlessly). The real way out is HIDDEN.
# This script deletes nothing and touches nothing outside this room.

cat <<'EOF'

  ____________________________
 /                            \
 |  You reach for the chest... |
 \____________________________/

SNAP!  The lid was a MIMIC's jaws!  It was a TRAP all along!

EOF

if [[ -z $HP ]]; then
	echo -e "The trap lunges at you -- but you never set your HP to play!\n"
else
	(( HP -= 2 ))
	echo -e "The mimic snaps shut on your hand. You take 2 damage."
	echo -e "Your HP is: $HP\n"
fi

cat <<'EOF'
But take heart: this is only a trick of the dungeon.

NOTHING on your real disk was touched. No files were deleted.

Your treasures -- and your home -- are exactly as you left them.

  >> Retreat now:           « cd .. »
  >> Then look before you leap. The careless open chests blindly.
  >> The wise INSPECT first ( file / head -n 1 ) and reveal the
     hidden path with « ls -a ».

The true way out of this room was never the shiny, obvious one.
EOF
